From 61d2836893a865b4e86a6a1d3ddedd24c5927cd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:48:56 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(agent): make boolean config options session-scoped

A switch -- Fast mode today, Ultracode once the adapter exposes it as one --
now applies to the session it was flipped in and nothing else. Two things
used to carry it further, and both are removed for booleans only:

  * 0010's Shift-click persisted a switch as the entry's default, so every
    new thread started with it. Defaults are a feature of the list options
    (model, mode, effort), where "from now on" is a real choice; a toggle
    has no default to set. The switch tooltip now says "Applies to this
    session only" instead of teaching the gesture.

  * 0036 recorded each thread's last state and replayed it on reopen, so a
    thread left with a switch on came back with it on. `snapshot` no longer
    records booleans, and a boolean already sitting in a record written
    before this patch is ignored on load, so no existing thread re-arms one.

Why the scope matters: Ultracode tells the model that token cost is not a
constraint and runs standing multi-agent orchestration. Claude Code's CLI
(`/effort ultracode on|off`, "this session only") and the VS Code extension
both keep it per session. Carried into new threads, or re-armed on reopen,
it would spend on work nobody asked to run that way.

What still applies to a switch: a `default_config_options` boolean written
by hand in settings.json, on a new session. Since 0.6.1_p20261021 not on a
reopened one: nothing is recorded for a switch, and a reopen applies no
entry default (0036 follows upstream 3c8e3b5a01), so a reopened thread keeps
the agent's value. Only the UI stops writing one.

Not changed: the native agent's thinking-mode button keeps 0010's
Shift-click; it is not an ACP config option.

Tests: `load_ignores_a_recorded_toggle` (red without the load-side filter:
`web_search: true` was sent), the snapshot test now pins that booleans are
skipped, and the recorder and round-trip tests that asserted a recorded
boolean were rewritten to the new contract -- the round trip now expects the
agent's value on reopen (the entry default before 0.6.1_p20261021). agent_servers 150 passed; config_options 6 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
